#Introduction
Build a PLM-IQ PLM-IQ
 that indexes BOMs, cost sheets, SAP-style documents, engineering change notices, and PDFs. Implement layout-aware chunking, BM25 plus vector retrieval, RRF, reranking, metadata filters (tenant, product, revision), and source citations.

#Data - folder plm_enterprise_corpus
 
100,000+ parts and 10,000+ assemblies
Deep hierarchical BOMs (up to 10 levels)
Revision history and supersession chains
AML/AVL (approved manufacturer/vendor lists)
ECR/ECO workflows with before/after states
CAD metadata and drawing references
Manufacturing routings and work instructions
Test reports, quality records, and inspection results
Compliance documents (RoHS, REACH, etc.)
Supplier quotations and historical pricing
Synthetic emails, change discussions, and support tickets
PDFs containing tables, images, and scanned text to exercise OCR and layout-aware chunking
Cross-linked metadata (tenant, program, plant, product family, release status)

That style of corpus is excellent for validating BM25, semantic search, hybrid retrieval, RRF, reranking, citation quality, and complex enterprise question answering.


